WHY THIS IS RESULT-BEARING:
`sentenceCodes` is only an opaque constructor. There are no equations relating
it to W's character sequences or spaces. `wordsVals` is also opaque. The bridge
is the only connection from the input projection to the word list that drives
the loop and final result; no bridge-free universal connection theorem exists.

FALSE-CONCLUSION / OPPOSITE-INTERPRETATION WITNESS:
Let W0 = ["aa", "bbb", "cccc"], which satisfies validWords and has modeled
sentence length 11. Interpret the otherwise unconstrained
sentenceCodes(W0) as concrete codes("x"). Then Python and the supplied fixed
split semantics return ["x"], while the candidate bridge returns W0. The
conclusion ["aa","bbb","cccc"] = "x".split() is false.

